1-"""Statistics A, B and C of PREREGISTRATION.md on the downloaded sample, and the gate.
2-
3-Every decision uses only what was known when a trade printed: its market, category, price,
4-size and the direction of the taker. Markets are selected, and assigned to a period, on
5:`latest_expiration_time`, fixed at listing. The outcome enters only as the settlement value of
6-the maker's position, and the settlement date only as a cluster label.
7-
8-All per-print work happens in a DuckDB file on disk with a memory cap. Strings are replaced by
9-integer codes before any large aggregation, and taker orders are built with aggregations and
10-joins rather than window functions, so that the work spills to disk instead of failing when the
11-sample is larger than memory. pandas only sees one row per cell.
12-"""
